WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:04.800
After months of theories and debates about
what Marvel Studios was planning for the next

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:10.080
phase of their cinematic universe, studio
head Kevin Feige dropped some major news at

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:13.400
Comic-Con, laying out two years worth of film
and television projects.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:17.400
Here's a potentially spoiler-filled look at
what we can expect in Marvel Studios' Phase

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:17.900
4.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:22.640
After the universe-shaking events of Avengers:
Endgame, fans were wondering just where the

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:23.840
MCU would go from here.

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:28.720
So it's no surprise to learn that the studio
is dedicating Phase 4 to introducing new characters

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:33.020
and ideas, and expanding the idea of what
the MCU is and can do.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:37.610
2020 will see the release of Black Widow,
a flashback film set between Captain America:

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:41.890
Civil War and Avengers: Infinity War, as well
as Eternals, which introduces a whole new

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:48.160
mythos to the MCU. 2021 will also introduce
viewers to a new hero, Shang-Chi, as well

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:52.340
as deliver Marvel's first horror film with
the Doctor Strange sequel, and re-invent the

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:55.220
god of thunder yet again in Thor: Love and
Thunder.

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:59.440
And Marvel will also be expanding into television
with a slate of new shows on the upcoming

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:03.430
Disney+ streaming service shows that will
closely tie in with the films.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:07.400
With all that going on, it's no wonder there
wasn't room for a new Avengers film making

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:10.980
Phase 4 the first phase without an Avengers
blockbuster anchoring it.

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:15.420
The next Marvel movie to hit theaters will
be the long-awaited Black Widow solo film,

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:19.410
and Feige revealed a ton of exciting details
including the fact that part of the film takes

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:20.380
place in Budapest.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:24.460
Maybe we'll finally learn what happened to
Natasha the last time she was there!

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:27.820
"Just like Budapest all over again!"

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:30.580
"You and I remember Budapest very differently!"

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:33.060
And there was also some exciting casting news.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:38.060
Florence Pugh, who recently dazzled audiences
in Midsommar, appeared in the teaser trailer

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:42.780
as a fellow secret agent named Yelena who
has a strained relationship with Natasha.

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:48.120
It seems very likely that Pugh's character
is Yelena Belova, who was Black Widow's successor

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:48.980
in the comics.

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:53.440
Given Natasha's fate in Avengers: Endgame,
could this be a tease of things to come?

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:58.200
Plus, fan favorite Stranger Things actor David
Harbour was on hand, revealing that he will

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:03.700
be playing Alexei Shotakov, better known as
the Red Guardian, the Soviet Union's counterpart

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:04.840
to Captain America.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:08.950
He shares more than just a homeland with Natasha,
though in the comics, they were once married!

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:10.360
Harbour told Entertainment Weekly,

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:14.019
"In a way he’s a super-soldier, but he’s
also a very complicated guy.

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:17.020
He has a lot of flaws, a lot of idiosyncrasies.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:18.900
It’s a very rich character."

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:22.920
And the teaser also confirmed rumors that
Black Widow will be battling the villainous

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:23.700
Taskmaster.

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:26.520
Just who will be playing Taskmaster is still
up in the air.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.980
Could he actually be Red Guardian in disguise?

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:30.560
Or someone entirely different?

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:32.080
We'll just have to wait and see!

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:36.560
One of the biggest surprises of Comic-Con
was the shock announcement that not only is

00:02:36.569 --> 00:02:41.650
Natalie Portman returning to the MCU as Jane
Foster, she'll be gaining the powers of Thor

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:42.140
as well!

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:47.860
Directed by Taika Waititi, who helmed the
fan favorite Thor: Ragnarok, the fourth movie

00:02:47.879 --> 00:02:52.319
in the franchise called Thor: Love and Thunder
will be based in part on a recent run of comics

00:02:52.319 --> 00:02:57.769
that featured Jane becoming the new Thor after
the old one was found to be no longer worthy

00:02:57.769 --> 00:02:59.240
of wielding Mjolnir.

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:02.520
"You're all not worthy."

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:06.040
And she's not the only fan favorite powerhouse
returning to the franchise.

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:10.540
Tessa Thompson's Valkyrie will be back and
she may have a new lady love interest.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:15.510
After Avengers: Endgame, Feige announced that
Marvel would feature, quote, "prominent LGBT

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:20.159
heroes," and Thompson told the comic-Con crowd
that Valkyrie, who succeeded Thor as the leader

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:24.629
of the Asgardian people in Avengers: Endgame,
would be at the forefront of that push.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:25.620
She explained:

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:29.980
"First of all, as king, as new king [of Asgard],
she needs to find her queen.

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:31.540
So that will be the first order of business."

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:37.100
2016's Doctor Strange was a solid film, but
critics dinged it for sticking a little too

00:03:37.109 --> 00:03:41.860
closely to the Iron Man story formula: arrogant
rich guy falls victim to a surprise accident

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:45.829
and is forced to rebuild his outlook using
new tools, etc. etc.

00:03:45.829 --> 00:03:49.719
This was especially surprising considering
the film's director, Scott Derrickson, was

00:03:49.719 --> 00:03:53.659
best known for horror films like Sinister
and The Exorcism of Emily Rose.

00:03:53.659 --> 00:03:57.699
Well, that horror background may finally to
pay off, as Derrickson revealed that Doctor

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:02.040
Strange in the Multiverse of Madness is going
to be the MCU's first horror film.

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:06.879
And there's another unexpected twist: Elizbeth
Olsen's Scarlet Witch will co-star in the

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:10.480
film, which will tie into her Disney+ TV series,
WandaVision.

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:11.720
It's all coming together!

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.480
That wasn't the only surprise announcement
regarding WandaVision.

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:21.200
Besides Olsen and co-star Paul Bettany, who
is reprising his role as Vision, Marvel revealed

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:25.580
that Dear White People's Teyonah Parris will
be appearing in the show as Monica Rambeau.

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:29.880
That name should sound familiar: the character,
who is the daughter of fighter pilot Maria

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:32.860
Rambeau, previously appeared as a child in
Captain Marvel.

00:04:33.129 --> 00:04:37.200
And Wanda's fellow avenger Hawkeye is also
going to be connecting with the younger generation

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:41.139
on Disney+, as it was officially confirmed
that the series Hawkeye will feature Jeremy

00:04:41.139 --> 00:04:45.581
Renner's archer Clint Barton passing on his
skills to the new Hawkeye, Kate Bishop, in

00:04:45.581 --> 00:04:47.140
a storyline from the comics.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:48.280
Renner told the crowd,

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:52.060
"I get to teach someone else how to be a superhero
without superpowers."

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:57.260
Marvel also announced details for the upcoming
martial arts flick Shang-Chi and the Legend

00:04:57.260 --> 00:04:58.220
of the Ten Rings.

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:03.360
Chinese-Canadian actor Simu Liu will be playing
the title role, while Awkwafina will be appearing

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:04.500
in an undefined role.

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:10.380
And Chinese superstar Tony Leung is poised
to play long time Iron Man villain the Mandarin,

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:14.760
who in the comics wields the power of advanced
alien technology shaped into 10 rings.

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:18.870
Of course, a different version of the Mandarin
appeared in Iron Man 3, but it turned out

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:22.140
to be an actor named Trevor Salttery, played
by Ben Kingsley.

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:26.360
Marvel later released a short film teasing
that there is a real Mandarin out there somewhere.

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:30.659
And there's a good chance that Leung's version
of the character will be Shang-Chi's father:

00:05:30.659 --> 00:05:35.479
in the comics, Shang-Chi dedicated his life
to defeating his supervillain father Fu Manchu,

00:05:35.479 --> 00:05:39.069
but since Marvel doesn't own the rights to
that character, the Mandarin could make for

00:05:39.069 --> 00:05:42.020
a cool if only slightly less problematic replacement.

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:46.160
The Ten Rings have been teased since the very
beginning of the MCU in the first Iron Man

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:49.600
film, so it will be awesome to finally see
that plot thread pay off.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:51.880
"Who are these people?"

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:55.020
"They are your loyal customers, sir.

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:57.310
They call themselves the Ten Rings."

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:02.760
Maybe the biggest jawdropper of the whole
convention, though, came during Feige's closing

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:03.260
comments.

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:08.400
First, he teased a bunch of projects beyond
Phase 4 including Fantastic Four and the X-Men.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:09.120
Feige said,

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:11.860
"There's a lot of other stuff we didn't get
to talk about today.

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:14.610
We didn't even mention that we're making Black
Panther 2.

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:17.600
We didn't mention the fact that Guardians
of the Galaxy 3 is coming.

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:20.880
We didn't have time to talk about Captain
Marvel 2, by the way.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:23.620
I didn't even have time to talk about the
Fantastic Four.

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:26.020
And there's no time left to talk about mutants."

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:29.360
But there was time to talk about one more
thing: Blade.

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:36.039
Yes, in a true mic drop moment, Feige welcomed
two-ime Oscar winner Mahershala Ali onto the

00:06:36.039 --> 00:06:41.530
stage to reveal that the onetime Copperhead
actor from Luke Cage will be playing Blade

00:06:41.530 --> 00:06:44.740
in a reboot of the classic Wesley Snipes action
franchise.

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:49.120
With any luck, they'll make sure to definitely
include Blade's classic, iconic catch-phrase:

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:53.580
"Some m----------- are always trying to ice
skate uphill."

